Subject: [PATCH] rtl837x: allow the backported pcs_get_state neg_mode ABI

The MTK Linux 6.12 branch backports the three-argument pcs_get_state API.
Let the package detect that ABI in its actual phylink.h rather than relying
only on LINUX_VERSION_CODE. Native old kernels retain the old prototype.

--- a/src/rtl8372n.c
+++ b/src/rtl8372n.c
@@ -668,5 +668,5 @@
-#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 18, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE
+#if defined(RTL837X_PCS_GET_STATE_HAS_NEG_MODE) || KERNEL_VERSION(6, 18, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE
 static void rtl8372n_sds_pcs_get_state(struct phylink_pcs *pcs, unsigned int neg_mode,
 				 struct phylink_link_state *state)
 #else
 static void rtl8372n_sds_pcs_get_state(struct phylink_pcs *pcs,
